WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:11.470
Families often make other foods like mashed potatoes, sweet potatoes, cranberry sauce and vegetable casseroles.

2
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.210
A casserole is a dish that cooks slowly in an oven.

3
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.170
And do not forget about the gravy.

4
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:30.050
This rich sauce is made from the fatty liquid that comes off the turkey as it cooks.

5
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:37.010
People cover their turkey meat, stuffing and mashed potatoes with gravy.

6
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.370
The meal does not end with the turkey, stuffing, and side dishes, though.

7
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.790
For some people, the best part of the meal is dessert.

8
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:55.210
The quintessential Thanksgiving dessert is pie.

9
00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:09.870
Pumpkin, cherry, apple or pecan pie are all great ways to finish off a Thanksgiving meal...if you are not too full of food by that point!

10
00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:17.090
Some Americans must travel long distances to be with their families.

11
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:26.610
In fact, the Sunday after Thanksgiving is the busiest travel day of the entire year.

12
00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:33.150
This is usually when people return home from family gatherings.

13
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.330
Not everyone can make the return home each Thanksgiving.

14
00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:54.750
So, young people living in cities away from their hometowns sometimes celebrate “Friendsgiving” -- a Thanksgiving meal with their friends instead of their family.

15
00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:02.090
They gather at someone’s apartment or house and have a “potluck.”

16
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:09.850
This is a meal where everyone who is invited brings food to share with others.

17
00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:18.330
Thanksgiving is a big day for television, games and other entertainment.

18
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:26.650
One tradition is the television broadcast of Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade.

19
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:31.170
It takes place each year in New York City.

20
00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:40.610
Workers of the Macy’s store on Herald Square organized the first parade in 1924.

21
00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:49.650
Many of the workers were immigrants and wanted to hold a big parade like the ones in Europe.

22
00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:55.750
So, they dressed in costumes and borrowed some animals from the zoo.

23
00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:59.310
They also carried small balloons that floated just overhead.

24
00:02:59.160 --> 00:02:55.750
Many professional American football games are also played on Thanksgiving.

25
00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:55.750
Fans of the sport enjoy relaxing and watching a game or two after eating a big Thanksgiving meal.
